  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user\'s provided JSON schema. I\'ve noted the \'title\' and \'summary\' fields within the root object and the required data types. This forms the foundation for understanding the desired input structure. I need to fully understand this JSON schema specification, to begin to understand how to proceed.\n\n\n**Interpreting the User\'s Intent**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user\'s intent. The core request is clear: I need to build a web application that takes a JSON file of quiz questions (structured as described) as input and presents them in a game-like format, similar to Kahoot. I\'m focusing on the implied requirements regarding user interaction and game flow.\n\n\n**Defining Clean Code Standards**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing code clarity and maintainability. I\'m focusing on clean, modular code that\'s easy to read, understand, and extend. I\'m also considering user experience and responsiveness across all devices, ensuring a user-friendly and intuitive UX design. This game *must* be fun! I have some ideas for content to include: Sony WH-1000XM5, AI Tech Trivia, and Space Exploration.\n\n\n**Developing Feature Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on two key enhancements. First, I\'m integrating an AI-powered auto-generator using Gemini 3.6 Flash, enabling users to generate quiz JSON files by simply inputting a product name, topic, or article content. Second, I\'m designing an interactive visual quiz editor within the UI, allowing question creation, editing of options, time limits, difficulty, hints, and explanations, and exporting back to JSON. I need to make these intuitive to use.\n\n\n\n**Designing Game Interaction Features**\n\nI am now outlining in detail the core game mechanics. I plan to use the Web Audio API to implement music options with synthesized beats. I\'ve designed a score multiplier system based on answer speed and a streak counter for added excitement. Additionally, I\'m thinking about a \"hint\" drawer, difficulty indicators, and a live feedback screen with animations, score reveals, explanations, and answer statistics. I\'ve also planned two game modes: Solo Challenge and Host/Class Presentation.\n\n\n**Refining Game Mode Details**\n\nI\'m now refining the game mode design. I plan to include a Speed Run mode with half the time and double the points, along with a Practice mode that offers unlimited time, visible hints, and instant feedback. I\'m also planning post-game features, including an animated Kahoot-style podium with celebratory animations, performance statistics, and an answer review that shows selected vs. correct answers with explanations. I\'m also considering export options for the game summary and the updated JSON. I will provide audio toggle, and player scoreboards!\n\n\n**Structuring the File System**\n\nI\'m now detailing the file system architecture. I\'ve defined strict JSON schema definitions in `/src/types.ts` that match the user request. Additionally, I\'ve created sample quizzes in `/src/constants/samples.ts` to exactly match that schema. Web Audio API sound generator is in `/src/utils/audio.ts` for timer ticks, chimes, victory fanfare, and upbeat synth, with the validator in `/src/utils/jsonValidator.ts`. I am adding components such as `/src/components/Header.tsx`, `/src/components/JsonImportModal.tsx`, and `/src/components/QuizEditor.tsx`. I am also working on the game in `/src/components/Game/`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 616295810
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
